If the year does not fall into any of these ranges, print “Invalid Birth Year”.

', N'Easy', N'["1900 <= birthYear <= 2100", "Only integer input is expected", "Output must match the format exactly, including spaces and punctuation"]', 1, CAST(N'2025-10-16T00:47:00.270' AS DateTime), 1, NULL, NULL, 0, N'["Use conditional statements (if-else) to check which range the input year belongs to.", "Pay close attention to formatting of the final output \u2014 even a small change may cause a mismatch.", "Consider how you\u2019ll handle birth years outside the defined generation ranges."]', 1, 256, N'["Expected Time Complexity: O(1)", "Expected Space Complexity: O(1)", "Concept Focus: Conditional Statements and Output Formatting"]', N'["Primary Concept: Conditional Logic", "Related Concept: Range Checking and Control Flow", "Core Skill: Decision Making based on numerical input", "Educational Intent: Helps beginners learn how to classify input data using conditions and generate formatted output."]')
